03:23:36.534 NOT AUTHENTICATED: the game socket carries no credentials, so anyone who
03:23:36.535   connects is served as whichever account the claim or the fallback names.
03:23:36.535   The launcher checks a password before staking a claim; this socket does not.
03:23:36.535   See docs/launcher.md.
03:23:36.535 CLIENT TOKEN (0x0073): this server now READS the identity string the client carries
03:23:36.535   and resolves the account from it - a credential on the wire instead of an
03:23:36.535   inference about a socket. Every 0x0073 is logged with its length, so a run says
03:23:36.535   whether the client carried anything at all.
03:23:36.535   A MapleCW token is 26 characters of uppercase base32. An EMPTY identity is what
03:23:36.535   every capture before 2026-08-29 carried and what every reconnect sends - it is not
03:23:36.536   a refusal, and the weaker rules still decide. A WRONG or SPENT one downgrades the
03:23:36.536   connection to the fallback account, because a credential that can be skipped by
03:23:36.536   presenting a bad one is not a credential.
03:23:36.536   This authenticates the LOGIN socket only. 0x0073 has never appeared on a channel
03:23:36.536   connection, so the game socket is unchanged.
03:23:36.536 MIGRATION BINDING IS OFF (--bind-migrations). A migration is claimed by the
03:23:36.536   character id the connecting client ASSERTS, and nothing checks that the
03:23:36.536   connection has any right to it - so any connection to a channel port can
03:23:36.536   claim any character's pending migration by naming it. No race is needed.
03:23:36.536   The mechanism to close this is built and tested; it needs the hook to send
03:23:36.536   the session token on the channel socket before it can be switched on.
